body:
This is a feature proposal for instantsearch.js.

## Rationale

With React-InstantSearch we’ve added the possibility to provide a complete custom rendering of the component. We want to provide the same kind of possibility for our instantsearch.js users with the following in mind:

* bigger liberty for our users
* less maintenance for us (less option to add when there is a new use case)
* more thought leadership through constrained best practices).

## Proposed API

Apply the same connector approach to the widgets provided by instantsearch.js:

```js
var customMenu = connectMenu(function(opts, isFirstRendering) {
  // this function is called during the `init` and `render` parts of the widget lifecycle
  
  // isFirstRendering is true when it is called from `init`
  
  // opts contains all the options now provided to the our current rendering. This could be later clean up if we decide to support less templates and css customization.
});

instantsearch.addWidget(customMenu({
  container: '#brands',
  attributeName: 'brands',
  limit: 3,
}));
```

*This new implementation is only a pattern to apply on the widgets, it does not impact the current architecture. ~~It should also be fully compatible with the current instantsearch.js implementations~~ It has some impact on the current implementations of widgets, therefore it'll be released as part of a v2.*

## Steps

* \[x] Update all the widgets with the new pattern
* \[x] test connectors and make the first rendering consistent
* \[x] Iteration 2 (decouple view and business logic)
* \[x] Propagate widget configuration to view
* \[x] Document the newly added connectors
